        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "policy: repair denied gateway http endpoints",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Stack on #99720 to add the next policy doctor repair slice.\n- Classify `policy/gateway-http-endpoint-enabled` as an automatic narrowing repair.\n- Wire `doctor --fix` to set the exact reported denied Gateway HTTP endpoint `enabled` paths to `false`.\n- Leave URL-fetch allowlist findings manual; this PR only disables denied endpoints and preserves nested endpoint config.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed:\n`doctor --fix` can now repair denied Gateway HTTP endpoint findings by disabling the reported endpoint paths while preserving nested endpoint options such as URL-fetch settings.\n\nReal environment tested:\nWindows PowerShell in `C:\\src\\openclaw-policy-gateway-http-push`, current PR head `e1061f6991aa85fcc5c37844cc3b6f08a904a384`, stacked on #99720 head `c51bc971eb39d185ec2ad2633abdd0814e14070b`.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n1. `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD`\n2. Inspected the focused diff for the five touched policy doctor files.\n\nEvidence after fix:\nThe committed slice is +70/-2 across five files. The new test `repairs denied gateway HTTP endpoint findings` covers disabling `chatCompletions` and `responses`, verifies both repair change messages, checks no remaining findings, and verifies nested endpoint config remains intact. `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD` exited 0.\n\nObserved result after fix:\nThe repair path uses `setFindingConfigValues(..., \"enabled\", false)` for `policy/gateway-http-endpoint-enabled`, so only the reported endpoint `enabled` fields are narrowed.\n\nWhat was not tested:\nThis checkout has no `node_modules`, so I did not rerun Vitest locally after the final restack. GitHub CI is running on the pushed PR head.\n\n## Stack\n\n- Stacked on #99720 / #99700 / #99690 / #99686 / #99121.\n- Keep draft until #99720 is merged or this branch is rebased onto `main`.",
